  {"workspace_id":null,"slug":"molokhia-chicken-homemade","name_ar":"ملوخية بالفراخ","name_en":"Egyptian molokhia stew with chicken","description_ar":"ملوخية بطشة توم وسمنة ومعاها فراخ من غير جلد أو عضم. الحصة شاملة نصيبها من الفراخ، من غير رز أو عيش.","calories_kcal_per_100g":71.9,"protein_g_per_100g":9.45,"carbs_g_per_100g":2.42,"fat_g_per_100g":2.77,"fiber_g_per_100g":0.66,"origin":"seed","origin_note":"Home version adapted and compared from https://amiraspantry.com/mulukhia-aka-jews-mallow/ ; https://www.supermama.me/posts/الملوخية-بالفراخ . Compared leaf/broth ratios and Arabic chicken inclusion. Chose 500 g fresh leaves with about 1 litre retained broth and 800 g raw skinless boneless meat. Every portion includes chicken. Weights in grams are this batch's explicit household conversions/adaptations, not claimed source measurements. Nutrition is calculated only from the linked foods and finished weight; no website calorie panel is used. Ingredient proxies are nutrition-only mappings identified in ingredient notes; cook with the named actual ingredient. Dukkah, where present, approximates missing dry spices and is not a prescribed nut addition. \nYield: Six 350 g combined servings. About 600 g cooked skinless boneless chicken plus 1500 g molokhia/broth/onion/tasha = 2100 g. Begin with 1100 ml water, retain broth and chicken juices, and adjust to about 1 litre broth before adding leaves. Portion must include one-sixth chicken and one-sixth soup, not soup alone. Estimated edible finished weight, not measured; weigh the cooked batch to refine the estimate. Water and salt are omitted from nutrient ingredients; their retained mass is included in yield. Side bread/rice is excluded unless listed.","confidence":"medium","review_flags":["quantities_vary_by_household","yield_estimated","ingredient_proxy"],"meal_tags":["lunch","dinner"],"finished_weight_g":2100,"prep_minutes":20,"cook_minutes":55,"youtube_video_id":null,"is_active":true,"portions":[{"name_ar":"طبق","weight_