  {"workspace_id":null,"slug":"om-ali-croissant-homemade","name_ar":"أم علي بالكرواسون","name_en":"Homemade Om Ali with croissants","description_ar":"أم علي بيتية بكرواسون سادة محمص ولبن وقشطة ومكسرات وزبيب، من غير عجينة جاهزة إضافية.","calories_kcal_per_100g":188.61,"protein_g_per_100g":4.57,"carbs_g_per_100g":19.03,"fat_g_per_100g":10.96,"fiber_g_per_100g":1.15,"origin":"seed","origin_note":"Home version adapted and compared from https://amiraspantry.com/egyptian-dessert-omm-ali-om-ali-or-alis-mom/ ; https://amiraspantry.com/rice-p-easy-creamy-rice-pudding/ . Om Ali source explicitly permits toasted croissants instead of puff pastry. Selected that actual variant because puff pastry/Om Ali flakes are absent; cream, nuts, raisins and sugar are explicitly weighed, compared with rice-pudding dairy choices. Weights in grams are this batch's explicit household conversions/adaptations, not claimed source measurements. Nutrition is calculated only from the linked foods and finished weight; no website calorie panel is used. Ingredient proxies are nutrition-only mappings identified in ingredient notes; cook with the named actual ingredient. Dukkah, where present, approximates missing dry spices and is not a prescribed nut addition. \nYield: Six 250 g desserts. Starting ingredients 1540 g become 1500 g through about 40 g net evaporation during toasting and brief baking. Milk absorption softens pastry but does not add a second hydration mass. All milk is poured into the dish, not served as an uncounted side jug. No extra butter/ghee/oil: croissant fat and 100 g cream are already counted. Estimated edible finished weight, not measured; weigh the cooked batch to refine the estimate. Water and salt are omitted from nutrient ingredients; their retained mass is included in yield. Side bread/rice is excluded unless listed.","confidence":"medium","review_flags":["quantities_vary_by_household","yield_estimated","ingredient_proxy","cream_fat_varies"],"meal_tags":["snack"],"finished_we