  {"workspace_id":null,"slug":"shakshuka-homemade","name_ar":"شكشوكة بيتي","name_en":"Home-style Egyptian shakshuka","description_ar":"بيض في صلصة طماطم وبصل وفلفل، بزيت محسوب ومن غير عيش.","calories_kcal_per_100g":96.09,"protein_g_per_100g":4.99,"carbs_g_per_100g":4.83,"fat_g_per_100g":6.48,"fiber_g_per_100g":1.13,"origin":"seed","origin_note":"Home version adapted and compared from https://amiraspantry.com/shakshuka/ . Adapted the four-person tomato/pepper/egg method to two eggs per person, 650 g tomato and 35 g oil. No cheese garnish; egg allocation is a household adaptation. Weights in grams are this batch's explicit household conversions/adaptations, not claimed source measurements. Nutrition is calculated only from the linked foods and finished weight; no website calorie panel is used. Ingredient proxies are nutrition-only mappings identified in ingredient notes; cook with the named actual ingredient. Dukkah, where present, approximates missing dry spices and is not a prescribed nut addition. \nYield: Four 300 g servings each with two eggs. About 1443 g starting ingredients reduce to 1200 g through approximately 243 g evaporation, mainly from tomato. All oil retained; egg weights exclude shells. Equal partitioning of eggs and sauce is needed for reported portion protein. Estimated edible finished weight, not measured; weigh the cooked batch to refine the estimate. Water and salt are omitted from nutrient ingredients; their retained mass is included in yield. Side bread/rice is excluded unless listed.","confidence":"medium","review_flags":["quantities_vary_by_household","yield_estimated","ingredient_proxy"],"meal_tags":["breakfast","dinner"],"finished_weight_g":1200,"prep_minutes":15,"cook_minutes":25,"youtube_video_id":null,"is_active":true,"portions":[{"name_ar":"طبق","weight_g":300,"is_default":true}],"aliases":[{"kind":"alias_ar","alias":"شكشوكة"},{"kind":"alias_ar","alias":"بيض بالطماطم"}],"ingredients":[{"food_slug":"egg-raw","weight_g":400,"note_ar":"٨ ب