  {"workspace_id":null,"slug":"shorbet-adas-homemade","name_ar":"شوربة عدس أصفر","name_en":"Egyptian yellow lentil soup","description_ar":"شوربة عدس بالخضار والتوم والكمون، مضروبة ناعم وبزيت محسوب.","calories_kcal_per_100g":76.26,"protein_g_per_100g":3.8,"carbs_g_per_100g":11.72,"fat_g_per_100g":1.88,"fiber_g_per_100g":2.19,"origin":"seed","origin_note":"Home version adapted and compared from https://amiraspantry.com/red-lentil-soup-revisited/ ; https://turmat.no/oppskrifter/vegetar/shorbet-adas-egyptisk-linsesuppe . Compared Amira’s 200 g lentil pot and Hanan Abdelrahman’s Egyptian family vegetable soup. Selected yellow split lentils, omitted potato and used a measured onion-oil finish. Weights in grams are this batch's explicit household conversions/adaptations, not claimed source measurements. Nutrition is calculated only from the linked foods and finished weight; no website calorie panel is used. Ingredient proxies are nutrition-only mappings identified in ingredient notes; cook with the named actual ingredient. Dukkah, where present, approximates missing dry spices and is not a prescribed nut addition. \nYield: Six 350 g bowls. Starting 1024 g food ingredients plus 1500 ml water minus about 424 g evaporation = 2100 g. Lentils hydrate within the retained soup liquid, with no separate rice/pasta and no discarded cooking water. All 30 g finishing oil included. Estimated edible finished weight, not measured; weigh the cooked batch to refine the estimate. Water and salt are omitted from nutrient ingredients; their retained mass is included in yield. Side bread/rice is excluded unless listed.","confidence":"medium","review_flags":["quantities_vary_by_household","yield_estimated","ingredient_proxy"],"meal_tags":["lunch","dinner"],"finished_weight_g":2100,"prep_minutes":15,"cook_minutes":40,"youtube_video_id":null,"is_active":true,"portions":[{"name_ar":"طبق","weight_g":350,"is_default":true}],"aliases":[{"kind":"alias_ar","alias":"شوربة عدس"},{"kind":"alias_ar","alias":"عدس اصفر"}],"ingredients":[{"food_slug":"lentils-yellow-dry","weight_g":300,"note_ar":null},{"food_slug":"onion-raw","weight_g":180,"note_ar":"وزن بعد التقشير"},{"food_slug":"carrot","weight_g":200,"note_ar":null},{"food_slug":"tomato","weight_g":250,"note_ar":"طماطم مضروبة أو مفرومة"},{"food_slug":"garlic-raw","weight_g":20,"note_ar":"توم مقشر"},{"food_slug":"sunflower-oil","weight_g":30,"note_ar":"الزيت اللي داخل في الأكل فعلا"},{"food_slug":"lemon-juice","weight_g":40,"note_ar":null},{"food_slug":"dukkah-dry","weight_g":4,"note_ar":"كمون مطحون؛ الدقة بديل لحساب القيمة الغذائية بس، استخدم التابل المكتوب"}],"steps":["اغسل العدس وحطه مع الجزر والطماطم ونص البصل وحوالي ١٥٠٠ مل مية.","خليه يغلي وبعدها وطي لحد العدس والخضار ما يطروا.","اضرب الشوربة بالخلاط اليدوي وظبط القوام بمية سخنة لو احتاجت.","شوح باقي البصل والتوم في الزيت، وضيفهم مع الكمون والملح للشوربة وخليها تغلي غلوة.","ضيف الليمون وقسمها على ٦ أطباق، من غير عيش محمر إضافي."]},
  {"workspace_id":null,"slug":"taameya-fried-homemade","name_ar":"طعمية بيتي مقلية","name_en":"Home-fried Egyptian fava bean taameya","description_ar":"طعمية بالفول المدشوش والخضرة والسمسم. كمية الزيت المحسوبة هي اللي مفترض فضلت في الأقراص بعد التصفية.","calories_kcal_per_100g":267.63,"protein_g_per_100g":11.69,"carbs_g_per_100g":26.8,"fat_g_per_100g":13.62,"fiber_g_per_100g":11.14,"origin":"seed","origin_note":"Home version adapted and compared from https://amiraspantry.com/falafel/ ; https://www.arabamerica.com/recipe/egyptian-tamiya-falafel/ . Compared split-fava and whole-broadbean home mixtures. Scaled 180 g/15 patties to 300 g/25; leek is an own household adaptation. Absorbed oil and cooked patty mass are assumptions. Weights in grams are this batch's explicit household conversions/adaptations, not claimed source measurements. Nutrition is calculated only from the linked foods and finished weight; no website calorie panel is used. Ingredient proxies are nutrition-only mappings identified in ingredient notes; cook with the named actual ingredient. Dukkah, where present, approximates missing dry spices and is not a prescribed nut addition. \nYield: Five servings of five patties, 25 patties averaging 30 g cooked = 750 g. Ingredient mass before soaking is 670 g including 85 g retained frying oil. Net retained soaking water after frying is estimated 80 g; larger hydration is mostly offset by frying evaporation. Start with about 600 g frying oil; assume 85 g remains in drained patties and 515 g remains outside the food, excluded. This is 11.3% of final mass as added absorbed oil; not measured. Dry whole fava nutrition is a weak proxy for peeled split fava and overstates fibre. Prep excludes 8-hour soaking. Estimated edible finished weight, not measured; weigh the cooked batch to refine the estimate. Water and salt are omitted from nutrient ingredients; their retained mass is included in yield. Side bread/rice is excluded unless listed.","confidence":"low","review_fl